    "summary_insights": [
      "The company maintains a very strong liquidity position, with the current ratio improving from 3.82 to 4.50 in 2024.",
      "Cash reserves remain high at £644,612, although they decreased by 13.2% year-on-year, likely due to dividend payments exceeding annual profit.",
      "Net assets declined by 9.2% from £914,928 to £830,601, driven by a £164,500 dividend distribution which surpassed the year's profit of £80,173.",
      "The asset base is debt-free with zero long-term liabilities and no bank loans or overdrafts reported.",
      "Tangible fixed assets decreased by 22.6% to £200,721, primarily due to depreciation charges and a £30,000 disposal of plant and machinery.",
      "Working capital remains robust, with current assets covering current liabilities more than four times over, providing significant financial resilience."
